Full licence text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

This licence covers:
- the sense annotations (the "Sense" column in each data file)
- the instance identifiers (the "number" column) and Tweet IDs
- the sense labels and sense identifiers in the unified sense inventory,
  and any sense descriptions written by the authors in their own words
- the annotation guidelines
- the synthetic training data (Synthetic Training Data.zip)

Excluded third-party content (NOT covered by this licence):
- The "Text" column. CCOHA-derived contexts (T1: 1980–1999; T2: 2000–2009)
  are provided in lemmatised, randomised form only; the underlying corpus
  remains subject to the COHA terms of use (Davies, 2012).
- Twitter content (T3: 2010–2020) is not redistributed. Only Tweet IDs are
  released; tweets must be retrieved via the authorised X API, subject to
  X's developer terms.
- Dictionary sources (Oxford English Dictionary, Green's Dictionary of Slang,
  Online Slang Dictionary, Urban Dictionary). No verbatim dictionary entries
  or definitions are redistributed; these sources remain subject to their
  respective copyright.

If you use this dataset, please cite the BD-LSC paper.
